-- Migration for schema/047 (beeline-kgyd.4.11): an existing sample's changes are applied from the samples file, one
-- kind of change to a row of upload_sample_outcome. Comments only: no column, key or CHECK changes (the CHECKs
-- already admit applied, unchanged, refused and skipped).
COMMENT ON COLUMN upload_sample_outcome.unit IS '''row'' for a whole new row, made into a trap sample; for a change to an existing sample, the kind of change: method_dates, trap_count, specimen_count, collectors, coordinates, area (country, state and county) or place (locality). Part of the key, and never null, so the key has no null in it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN upload_sample_outcome.outcome IS 'pending: queued, not done. created: a trap sample was made from a new row. applied: a change to an existing sample was made. unchanged: nothing needed changing. refused: the row or change was checked when its turn came, or predicted when the file was applied, and a correction would not make it (detail says why). skipped: left alone on purpose, such as a look-alike that was not ticked, a kind of change that was not ticked, or the country, state and county that follow a point just set.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN upload_sample_outcome.payload IS 'What the job is to write, as JSON, worked out and checked when the upload was applied, including the person ids its collectors came to, and for a change to an existing sample the sampleVersion the file says and the cells it came from. The job writes exactly this, so it does not depend on the file or on matching names again. Null for what the claim settled itself (a held row, a kind not ticked, a change predicted to be refused), which is how the job tells work it did from work done at the claim.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN upload_applied.draft_count IS 'What was done, counted: for a volunteer''s file, the number of drafts written, one for each identification the preview listed; for staff''s samples file, the number of new rows and of changes to existing samples queued for the job (outcome pending when the upload was applied), not counting those left alone or refused when it was applied, which also have an upload_sample_outcome row.';
